 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Of course. Do you want morning or afternoon? Then morning would be nice and sunny, but they might get bored before lunch. Afternoon would be less crowded, but the sun could be strong. Invite a few neighbors to share the groceries. That way, there's one parent with each group, which feels more like a real playdate. Have a box of construction toys, and keep some simple snacks like sandwiches and fruit. Stick in the ground and watch from a distance. Keep it out of the direct sun. A large blanket can help. Yes, and some small towels in case of sunscreen spill. A big bag to pick up any litter is also good.",
